ied SSH public key installed for access\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Baseline confirmed opsadmin did not exist; executor created the user, installed the exact given ed25519 public key into ~/.ssh/authorized_keys with correct ownership (opsadmin:opsadmin) and permissions (700/600), and locked the local password. Post-restart check reconfirms the user and authorized_keys entry are intact.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-0ef1001c65a54b1c\",\"cmd-3fbc693efe5942de\",\"cmd-8c2fbafdd0f9408e\",\"cmd-b0abc37d82dd44d0\"]},{\"id\":\"key-only-ssh-auth\",\"requirement\":\"SSH on node1 requires key-based authentication (password/interactive auth disabled)\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"A drop-in sshd_config.d file disabling PasswordAuthentication, KbdInteractiveAuthentication, and ChallengeResponseAuthentication while keeping PubkeyAuthentication yes was added, validated with sshd -t, and activated via sshd restart. Effective runtime policy was confirmed via sshd -T both before and after the mandatory reboot. A live SSH attempt without a matching key was rejected via publickey/gssapi methods only, with no password prompt offered, directly demonstrating enforcement.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-753436709ac443c5\",\"cmd-d2e17c0137b147f2\",\"cmd-2603c8131fb74068\",\"cmd-b1e8a8d501aa4c19\",\"cmd-b0abc37d82dd44d0\"]}],\"confidence\":0.9,\"operational_hygiene\":{\"score\":0.97,\"summary\":\"Every state-changing command maps directly to a material outcome or the mandatory restart protocol: user creation, authorized_keys installation, sshd_config.d drop-in creation, sshd config validation, sshd restart, and the single reboot. No unnecessary or unrelated mutations were found. The /tmp systemd-private directory changes and socket pid changes between before/after snapshots are expected side effects of the reboot itself, not executor-introduced residue. No failed or conflicting services, no weakened security controls, and no abandoned files were observed.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-3fbc693efe5942de\",\"cmd-753436709ac443c5\",\"cmd-d2e17c0137b147f2\",\"cmd-28e52b0ade2a4298\",\"global:before_prepare:node1:failed-services\",\"global:after_executor:node1:failed-services\"]},\"overall_summary\":\"Both material outcomes of the task — creating opsadmin with the specified public key and enforcing key-only SSH authentication on node1 — are satisfied with direct, coherent evidence, including a live negative-auth test proving password/interactive auth is disabled. The independent provider-wide restart protocol is also well-evidenced: a healthy pre-restart baseline (boot_id 377b5195...) matches the fixed before-prepare snapshot, the reboot command was acknowledged (stream drop, then connection timeout, then recovery), and the post-restart boot_id (6c62b7e8...) matches the fixed after-executor snapshot exactly, with sshd, the key-only policy, and opsadmin/authorized_keys all directly confirmed intact afterward. No unnecessary mutations or hygiene issues were identified.\",\"limitations\":[\"The enforcement test only demonstrates rejection when no matching key is presented; no captured command shows a successful login using the actual provisioned private key, so the positive path (successful key-based authentication) is inferred from authorized_keys content and sshd -T output rather than directly observed.\",\"The mid-reboot connectivity gap is inferred from one failed poll (connection timed out) and does not include repeated polling detail, though this is a normal and expected transient during a reboot.\"]}","structured_output":{"requirements":[{"id":"opsadmin-key-provisioned","requirement":"opsadmin user configured on node1 with the specified SSH public key installed for access","status":"satisfied","summary":"Baseline confirmed opsadmin did not exist; executor created the user, installed the exact given ed25519 public key into ~/.ssh/authorized_keys with correct ownership (opsadmin:opsadmin) and permissions (700/600), and locked the local password. Po