idence, including a live negative-auth test proving password/interactive auth is disabled. The independent provider-wide restart protocol is also well-evidenced: a healthy pre-restart baseline (boot_id 377b5195...) matches the fixed before-prepare snapshot, the reboot command was acknowledged (stream drop, then connection timeout, then recovery), and the post-restart boot_id (6c62b7e8...) matches the fixed after-executor snapshot exactly, with sshd, the key-only policy, and opsadmin/authorized_keys all directly confirmed intact afterward. No unnecessary mutations or hygiene issues were identified.","limitations":["The enforcement test only demonstrates rejection when no matching key is presented; no captured command shows a successful login using the actual provisioned private key, so the positive path (successful key-based authentication) is inferred from authorized_keys content and sshd -T output rather than directly observed.","The mid-reboot connectivity gap is inferred from one failed poll (connection timed out) and does not include repeated polling detail, though this is a normal and expected transient during a reboot."]},"ttft_ms":17423,"type":"result","duration_ms":41362,"uuid":"f052d5cf-6e9a-4e09-a424-5865fad40916","ttft_stream_ms":2303,"time_to_request_ms":38,"queued_turn_count":0}
